  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation  $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=-\\frac{2}{3}$ for ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=-\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\text{arctan}(-\\frac{3}{2})=-(56.309\\,9\u2026)^{\u2218}\u2248-{56.310}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-{56.310}^{\u2218}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{\u2218}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={180}^{\u2218}+x={180}^{\u2218}-{56.310}^{\u2218}={123.690}^{\u2218},\\,\\,{x}_{2}={360}^{\u2218}+x={360}^{\u2218}-{56.310}^{\u2218}={303.690}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n123.690\\cdot 303.690\u224837\\,563\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.",
